international team of scientists to  include americans to visit the institute  of virology in wuhan and have total  and uncontrolled access to its personnel  so even if they've destroyed the  evidence we can at least take  the statements of people who were there  that's not what the world health  organization did last month and they  sent a team  in basically just to corroborate the  chinese story  that's just one thing though that should  be on the agenda item we should press  them on  their uh breaking their words and their  international commitments on hong kong  autonomy  and the genocide they're perpetrating  against religious and ethnic minorities  in western china  these are things that some biden  administration officials have raised  either in speeches or congressional  testimony but joe biden himself  has been very reticent to push china on  those issues and that's not a strong  signal  to send to chinese to china's leader xi  jinping  what should the u.s be doing about this  i mean  i certainly remember hong kong to be an  amazing  international business hub where  you felt that there was freedom you  certainly felt that there was  opportunity  i understand from my sources in hong  kong it is a  very bleak time right now in hong kong  should the u.s be responding  to how the ccp has handled things  yeah it's a terrible tragedy maria hong  kong has a vibrant  history of freedom and democracy and the  rule of law  and china committed to uphold that for  50 years in 1997 when they reclaimed  sovereignty over hong kong from the  united kingdom  and not even a quarter of a century into  that commitment  they broke it and they were pressing all  hong kongers now china should have to  pay  for all of these transgressions whether  it's violating its commitments about  hong kong  or committing genocide against its own  people or stealing our jobs and our  property  and using them to try to outpace us as  the world's economic  leader now how they pay for that is up  for us  so for instance one thing i've pressed  our generals on and our admirals on  in the armed service committee as of  late is that we need to be deploying as  many  ground-based missiles as possible to our  territories in the western pacific and  our allies  to hold china at risk they haven't faced  that for a long time  because we were constrained in an old  and outdated treaty with russia  but put a few hundred or more likely a  few thousand missiles in the western  pacific that can reach the chinese  mainland and will make the leaders in  beijing sweat a lot  we also have not heard president biden  say much about the uyghurs  and the genocide that is being committed  there so  we'll see if this comes up in this  meeting but i want to get your take on  the upcoming olympics there is uh  uh the olympics happening in uh 2022  and gordon chang tweeted this a friend  asked  will china collect dna samples  of the athletes and others at the  olympics if they are held in beijing  and he says you bet do you think that  the chinese communist party will collect  dna of our athletes  well i wouldn't put it past the chinese  communist party to undertake any kind of  spying or espionage against americans in  beijing  i think the international olympic  committee needs to try to move these  olympics out of china  they were awarded under different  circumstances when so many people still  took the china threat for granted  um and if barring that then i think we  need to seriously consider senator  romney's proposal  that we have an economic and diplomatic  boycott even if we send our athletes  athletes to compete americans don't go  to watch they don't spend money in  hotels and restaurants and sightseeing  american corporations don't sponsor  these games so hit china where it hurts  on these olympics in their pocketbook  but there needs to be consequences for  china's malign  actions not only against american  interest but against international peace  and stability more broadly  and its brutal repression of its own  people now let me ask you before you go  senator you are on the front lines in  terms of ensuring  that we have the agenda that will  lead to progress in america you've got  hr1  you've got a 1.9 trillion stimulus  you've got another package on the way  that's coming  including higher taxes a word about this  agenda  how do you see it  well i think it's a failed agenda it's a  radical agenda joe biden is simply  the front man for the far democratic  left that wants to spend trillions of  dollars  on their long-standing priorities wants  to rig the rules of our elections wants  to use  your tax dollars to elect democratic  candidates wants to pack the supreme  court and wants to make washington d.c  estate it's not popular and they're not  going to do it  can you do anything about it to stop it  well right now they don't have the votes  to pass it because it's so unpopular if  they've got divisions in their own party  they can't even pass most of these  things  through the house of representatives  much less the senate  all right senator it's good to have you  this evening thanks very much we will  catch up soon  senator tom cotton
 

